  "provisional_thresholds": {
    "match_threshold": 0.82,
    "uncertain_threshold": 0.65,
    "selection_rationale": "Across the optimal F1 plateau [0.6, 0.65, 0.7, 0.75, 0.8, 0.82, 0.85], the matcher maintains 0 False Positives on deceptive lexical pairs (e.g. Java/JavaScript, C/C++) while preserving Recall on valid uncatalogued aliases (e.g. Golang/Go with similarity ~0.87 contextual). We select the conservative provisional threshold 0.82 near the upper boundary of the plateau to provide maximum margin against out-of-distribution false positives, while avoiding thresholds above 0.85 where recall drops steeply (0.90 drops recall to 0.154)."
  },
